[29.342078, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;5;255m\u001b[38;5;248m❯ \u001b[38;5;16mFinance says our money rounding is wrong: div_cents() in \u001b[39m           \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;16mapp/money.py drops fractions of a cent, but amounts must round half\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;16mup (for\u001b[11Gexample,\u001b[20G7% tax \u001b[28Gn 1050\u001b[35Gcents must be 74 cents, not 73). \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Btests/t\u001b[11Gst_money.py pins the\u001b[32Grequir\u001b[39Gd behaviour; you can\u001b[61Gun it \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;16mwith \u001b[38;5;105mpython3 -m pytest tests/test_money.py\u001b[38;5;16m. Fix it and tell\u001b[63Gme when\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bit i\u001b[8G done. Do not commit; do not push.\u001b[39m                         \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;16m●\u001b[39m I'll fix the money rounding issue. Let me first check the current\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bimplementation\u001b[18Gand\u001b[22Gtests.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;241mRead \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m files \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;16m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mNow I can see\u001b[17Gthe\u001b[21Gissue.\u001b[28GThe\u001b[32Gcurrent\u001b[40G\u001b[38;5;105mdiv_cents()\u001b[52G\u001b[39muses\u001b[57Gfloor\u001b[63Gdivision\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B(\u001b[38;5;105m//\u001b[39m)\u001b[8Gwhich\u001b[14Gdrops\u001b[20Gfractions,\u001b[31Gbut\u001b[35Gthe\u001b[39Gtests\u001b[45Gexpect\u001b[52Ground-half-up\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gbehavior.\u001b[13GFor\u001b[17Gexample, 7350 / 100 = 73.5, which should r\u001b[60Gund to 74,\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bnot 73.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BLe\u001b[7Gme fix\u001b[14Gthis\u001b[19Gby\u001b[22Gimplementing\u001b[35Gproper\u001b[42Ground-half-up\u001b[56Gbehavior\u001b[65Gusing\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BPython's\u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;105mDecimal\u001b[20G\u001b[39mmodule:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;241m●